     1,
     "For a histogram you only supply an x variable. <div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>ggplot(z, aes(x=value, fill=variable)) + geom_histogram(position=position_dodge())</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Sep 28, 2012 at 9:04 AM, Sarita Paranjpe <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">heys...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div>ggplot(z, aes(x=variable, fill=variable, y=value)) + geom_histogram(position=&quot;dodge&quot;)</div></blockquote>\r\n\r\n</div><br></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
